@@ -53,6 +53,13 @@ For shader resources, pass the declared pipeline layout to the file compiler:
 Those declared inputs are reflected into the sidecar and must stay consistent
 with the SPIR-V interface.
 
+API 18 filters reflection at descriptor-set granularity using the compiler's
+actual user-SGPR layout: sets without a direct or indirect stage address are
+omitted, while every declared binding in an addressable set is retained. It
+also marks fragment binaries compiled with the alpha-to-one epilog so the
+native pipeline can reject state/shader mismatches, and omits push-constant
+and indirect-descriptor user SGPRs when the reflected interface uses neither.
+
 Reflection must describe every compiler-derived requirement needed for safe
 pipeline creation, including:
 
